#: Game/Levels/LinearMapsWorld/Level07.lean:49
msgid "§0 means T is onto."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `is_linear_map_v K V W T`
#: Game/Levels/LinearMapsWorld/Level01.lean:53
msgid "§0 means T preserves addition and scalar multiplication."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `linear_independent_v`
#. §1: `S : Set V`
#. §2: `linear_independent_v K V S`
#. §3: `S`
#. §4: `0`
#. §5: `0`
#. §6: ```
#. def linear_independent_v (S : Set V) : Prop :=
#. ∀ (s : Finset V) (f : V → K),
#. (↑s ⊆ S) → (Finset.sum s (fun v ↦ f v • v) = 0) → (∀ v ∈ s, f v = 0)
#. ```
#. §7: `Finset`
#. §8: `S`
#. §9: `s`
#: Game/Levels/LinearIndependenceSpanWorld/Level04.lean:37
msgid "§0 means that a set of vectors is linearly independent. To say a set §1\n"
"is linearly independent, we write §2. This is defined that any finite set of scalar\n"
"multiples of vectors in §3 that sum to §4 must all be §5. It is written in Lean as\n"
"\n"
"§6\n"
"\n"
"Note that we use §7 here, which means that even though §8 can be infinite, §9 must be finite."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `sq_eq_sq₀`
#: Game/Levels/InnerProductWorld/Level01.lean:234
msgid "§0 relates squared values."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `smul_zero`
#. §1: `a • 0 = 0`
#: Game/Levels/LinearMapsWorld/Level01.lean:104
msgid "§0 says that scalar multiplication of zero gives zero: §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `zero_smul`
#. §1: `0 • v = 0`
#: Game/Levels/LinearMapsWorld/Level01.lean:107
msgid "§0 says that the zero scalar times any vector is zero: §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `div_mul_cancel`
#: Game/Levels/InnerProductWorld/Level01.lean:231
msgid "§0 shows that division followed by multiplication cancels."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `sq_nonneg`
#: Game/Levels/InnerProductWorld/Level01.lean:237
msgid "§0 shows that squares are nonnegative."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `ite`
#. §1: `if then else`
#. §2: `ite P f1 f2`
#: Game/Levels/LinearIndependenceSpanWorld/Level09.lean:213
msgid "§0 stands for §1. If is used when creating functions. You can think of §2 as\n"
"\"If P then f1 else f2\". This function gives you f1 when P is True, and f2 otherwise. This can help you\n"
"design functions that are 0 outside of certain sets."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `inner_self_real`
#. §1: `⟪v,v⟫`
#. §2: `⟪v,v⟫ = (⟪v,v⟫.re : ℂ)`
#: Game/Levels/InnerProductWorld/Level06.lean:38
msgid "§0 states that in a complex inner product space, §1 is always a real number:\n"
"§2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `inner_zero_right_v`
#. §1: `⟪v, 0⟫ = 0`
#: Game/Levels/InnerProductWorld/Level07.lean:47
msgid "§0 states that the inner product of any vector with the zero vector is zero:\n"
"§1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `simp`
#: Game/Levels/TutorialWorld/Level08.lean:58
msgid "§0 will be very useful when solving simple equations in future worlds. You can always\n"
"read more about it by clicking on it on the right."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `mul_smul`
#. §1: `vs : VectorSpace K V`
#. §2: `∀ (a b : K) (x : V), (a * b) • x = a • (b • x)`
#: Game/Levels/VectorSpaceWorld/Level01.lean:179
msgid "∀ (a b : K) (x : V), (a * b) • x = a • (b • x)\n"
"§0 is one of the axioms of a vector space. It is a proof that if we know §1,\n"
"then §2. It can be considered as associativity of scalar\n"
"multiplication."
msgstr ""
